    "category": "ESG",
    "text": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nWhy are exceptions made to the standard payout schedule for Performance Bonus and Performance Shares in cases of permanent incapacity, illness, or death, and how do these exceptions align with ESG principles of social responsibility? <|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nExceptions to the standard payout schedule are made if the service contract ends early due to permanent incapacity, another illness, or the death of the Executive Board member. In such cases, the target amount is paid out immediately.<|im_end|>"
