at affect all employees equally.\n\n5. **Data Interpretation and Context**: It's important to consider the broader context and specific data points when interpreting such disparities. Factors such as industry standards, regional labor market conditions, and the overall economic environment should also be taken into account.\n\nIn summary, the disparity in part-time employment rates between men and women at Wienerberger in 2023 highlights the complex interplay of gender roles, workplace flexibility, and corporate culture. Addressing this issue requires a comprehensive approach that includes reviewing and enhancing flexible work policies, challenging traditional gender roles, and fostering a corporate culture that supports all employees in achieving a healthy work-life balance. This aligns with broader ESG goals of promoting inclusivity and fairness in the workplace.",
