ticeable changes in headcount at specific times of the year.\n   - **Cost Management:** Year-end adjustments might also reflect efforts to manage costs more effectively. For example, reducing headcount at the end of the year could be a way to align expenses with revenue targets or prepare for budget cycles.\n\nIn summary, the more evident personnel adjustments in the year-end headcount compared to average FTEs suggest that Wienerberger employs a dynamic approach to workforce management, capable of making swift adjustments to meet changing business requirements. This flexibility is crucial in today's rapidly evolving business environment.",
