tes. Providing survivor benefits is a clear demonstration of a company’s commitment to the social aspect of ESG, showing that the company prioritizes the welfare of its stakeholders beyond just its shareholders.\n\nIn summary, offering a portion of the pension to the spouse of a deceased Executive Board member is a way for companies to uphold their social responsibilities, enhance employee satisfaction, comply with legal standards, and align with broader ESG principles. This practice underscores the company’s commitment to the well-being of its employees and their families, reflecting positively on its overall CSR efforts.",
