tics, are also considered. Ensuring that suppliers adhere to sustainable practices can help in reducing the overall carbon footprint.\n\n7. **Renewable Energy Use**: The extent to which renewable energy sources are integrated into the production process is a critical factor. Using solar, wind, or hydroelectric power can significantly reduce CO₂ emissions compared to traditional fossil fuel-based energy.\n\n8. **Carbon Capture and Storage (CCS) Technologies**: Implementing CCS technologies can capture CO₂ emissions directly at the source and store them, preventing their release into the atmosphere.\n\nBy considering these factors, Wienerberger can better understand and manage its environmental impact, aligning with the EU Taxonomy's goals for sustainable economic activities. This approach not only helps in reducing CO₂ emissions but also supports broader sustainability efforts, such as resource efficiency and biodiversity conservation.",
