oring and managing energy use, HVAC systems, lighting, and other building operations can optimize performance and reduce waste.\n\n7. **Sustainable Materials**: Using recycled, recyclable, or low-impact materials in construction can reduce the overall carbon footprint of the building and promote circular economy principles.\n\n8. **Resilient Infrastructure**: Ensuring that critical infrastructure within buildings (such as electrical systems, heating, and cooling) is robust and can continue to function during disruptions caused by climate-related events.\n\n9. **Indoor Environmental Quality**: Improving indoor air quality through proper ventilation and the use of non-toxic materials can enhance occupant health and well-being, which is indirectly related to sustainability goals by promoting healthier living conditions.\n\nThese adaptations not only help in mitigating climate risks but also align with broader sustainability goals outlined in the EU Taxonomy, contributing to a more resilient and sustainable built environment.",
