teria. This includes qualitative and quantitative information about the extent to which their activities contribute to the environmental objectives.\n\n4. **EFRAG's Role**: The European Financial Reporting Advisory Group (EFRAG) has been tasked with developing draft EU Sustainability Reporting Standards (EU-SRS) that will complement the EU Taxonomy. These standards aim to provide guidance on how companies should report on sustainability-related information, including information relevant to the Taxonomy.\n\nIn summary, while the EU Taxonomy does not directly specify accounting standards, it relies on the consistent application of EFRAG and IFRS for financial reporting, alongside additional sustainability reporting requirements that are being developed to support the Taxonomy's objectives. Companies must ensure they comply with both the financial reporting standards and the new sustainability reporting requirements to accurately categorize and disclose their assets under the EU Taxonomy framework.",
