ile these financial indicators are not mandated by the regulation itself, they are often used by companies to provide a comprehensive picture of their sustainability efforts and the financial implications thereof. The exact requirements can vary based on the type of entity (e.g., financial institutions vs. non-financial corporations) and the specific activities being reported.\n\nFor precise guidance, companies should refer to the detailed guidelines provided by the European Commission and consult with legal and financial advisors familiar with the EU Taxonomy Regulation.",
