ce waste and recover valuable materials.\n\n6. **Digitalization and Smart Mobility Solutions:** Investments in digital platforms and smart mobility solutions that optimize traffic flow, reduce congestion, and encourage the use of shared mobility services, thereby lowering overall emissions.\n\nTo qualify under the EU Taxonomy, these investments must also meet the \"do no significant harm\" principle, ensuring that they do not cause significant negative impacts on other environmental objectives such as water and air pollution, biodiversity loss, and waste generation.\n\nIt's important for companies to conduct detailed assessments to ensure their CapEx projects meet the specific criteria outlined in the EU Taxonomy Regulation. This may involve working with sustainability consultants and using tools provided by the European Commission to evaluate the alignment of their activities.",
