 can also contribute to climate change mitigation.\n- **Sustainable IT Infrastructure:** Ensuring that the company’s IT infrastructure is energy-efficient and uses renewable energy sources, which can align with the taxonomy’s criteria for climate change mitigation.\n\nTo determine if TeamViewer’s specific activities meet the detailed criteria set out in the EU Taxonomy, it would be necessary to conduct a thorough assessment against the technical screening criteria provided in the Delegated Acts related to each environmental objective. This involves evaluating not only the direct impact of their products and services but also considering indirect impacts and ensuring that there are no significant negative effects on other environmental objectives.\n\nFor a precise alignment analysis, TeamViewer would likely need to consult the relevant Delegated Acts and possibly seek expert advice to ensure compliance and alignment with the EU Taxonomy standards.",
