 nuclear energy to qualify under the taxonomy, it must meet strict safety standards and have a plan for the management of radioactive waste. Similarly, for fossil gas activities to be considered, they must contribute to the transition towards a low-carbon economy and meet stringent environmental performance criteria.\n\nIn summary, while I cannot provide specific details about why SLISS MicroTec is exempt from the reporting forms under Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1214 without more context, the inclusion of nuclear energy and fossil gas in the EU Taxonomy reflects a broader policy approach aimed at supporting a sustainable transition while acknowledging the role these energy sources can play under certain conditions.",
