for data centers.\n\n5. **Regular Review and Reporting**: Finally, the company needs to regularly review its activities and report on how they comply with the DNSH principle. Transparency and continuous improvement are key aspects of adhering to the EU Taxonomy.\n\nThis analysis is critical under the EU Taxonomy framework because it ensures that economic activities labeled as sustainable truly contribute positively to environmental goals without causing significant harm elsewhere. It helps investors make informed decisions about where to allocate their funds, ensuring that capital flows support genuine sustainability efforts across all environmental objectives, not just one.",
