. **Resource Constraints**: Organizations may face resource constraints, including time, expertise, and technology, which can hinder their ability to meet the technical screening criteria for taxonomy alignment.\n\nAddressing these challenges typically involves enhancing training and guidance for preparers, improving data collection processes, ensuring compliance with updated standards, and leveraging advanced technologies to facilitate better alignment with the taxonomy. It also highlights the ongoing need for continuous improvement in financial reporting standards and practices to keep pace with evolving business environments and technological advancements.",
