employees on sustainability issues can lead to improved environmental performance and innovation in sustainable business practices. By recognizing these costs in the KPI, the regulation incentivizes organizations to allocate resources towards sustainability education and awareness, thereby fostering a culture of sustainability within the organization.\n\nIn summary, the requirement to include training costs in both the numerator and denominator of the OpEx KPI calculation under Delegated Regulation 2021/2178 enhances transparency and consistency in financial reporting while promoting investment in sustainability-related training. This approach aligns with the overarching objectives of the EU Taxonomy by encouraging organizations to develop the necessary skills and knowledge to operate sustainably and contribute positively to environmental goals.",
