reasons for discontinuing these investments is crucial. This helps maintain trust with stakeholders, including investors, customers, and regulators.\n\n4. **Alignment with Sustainable Finance Goals**: AGRANA must ensure that its new investments align with the EU Taxonomy criteria to continue benefiting from sustainable finance frameworks and to meet investor expectations for environmental performance.\n\n5. **Compliance with Regulatory Requirements**: Continued compliance with the EU Taxonomy Regulation requires ongoing assessment of all activities, including those that have been discontinued, to ensure accurate reporting and avoid any misalignment issues.\n\nIn summary, while the exact reasons for AGRANA's decision to discontinue investment in biogas and biofuels are not specified, the implications for taxonomy-aligned reporting are significant. The company needs to transparently report these changes and ensure that its remaining activities continue to meet the stringent criteria set out by the EU Taxonomy.",
