    "id": "train:000179:qa_pairs_factoid:0007",
    "problem": "Which fermentative substrates are utilized by Evonik for sustainable production processes?",
    "attempt": "Evonik Industries AG is a leading specialty chemicals company that focuses on innovation and sustainability. For their sustainable production processes, they utilize various fermentative substrates to produce bio-based products. Some of the key substrates include:\n\n1. **Sugar Cane**: Sugar cane is a common feedstock used in fermentation processes due to its high sugar content. It's an important raw material for producing bioethanol and other biochemicals.\n\n2. **Corn Starch**: Corn starch can be converted into sugars through enzymatic processes, which then serve as substrates for fermentation. This substrate is used in the production of various biobased products including organic acids and amino acids.\n\n3. **Lignocellulosic Biomass**: This includes materials like agricultural residues (e.g., corn stover, wheat straw) and wood chips. These materials are rich in cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin, which can be broken down into fermentable sugars using advanced pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis techniques.\n\n4. **Glycerol**: As a by-product of biodiesel production, glycerol can be used as a substrate in fermentation processes to produce valuable chemicals such as 1,3-propanediol.\n\n5. **Sugarcane Bagasse**: The fibrous residue left after sugarcane crushing can also be used as a substrate, especially when combined with other technologies to convert it into fermentable sugars.\n\nBy utilizing these renewable resources, Evonik aims to reduce dependency on fossil fuels and contribute to more sustainable industrial practices. Their approach not only focuses on the choice of substrates but also on optimizing the entire process chain from raw material sourcing to product manufacturing.",
