rs, and employees expect companies to take action on environmental issues. Demonstrating commitment through concrete actions like RECs and industry network participation can help meet these expectations.\n\n8. **Long-term Cost Savings**: While there might be initial investments required, the long-term benefits of reduced energy costs and potential revenue streams from selling excess renewable energy can outweigh these upfront costs.\n\nBy focusing on these initiatives, companies not only contribute to global efforts to combat climate change but also position themselves for long-term success in a rapidly evolving market where sustainability is becoming increasingly important.",
