not alter the total headcount but could influence the contractual stability and flexibility of the workforce.\n\nTo uncover these underlying dynamics, it would be necessary to analyze detailed data on individual employee records, including promotions, transfers, retirements, new hires, contract types, and working hours. This deeper analysis would reveal whether the workforce is truly stable or undergoing subtle yet significant transformations.",
